format session-log-v1
stamp 20260906.213313
editor Claude Code, Zed-class CLI on the pier
provider Anthropic
product Claude Code
role incense seat -- law, active-designing, iterative review, the captain's hat
modality text
model claude-opus-5
model_status active runtime reported by the harness environment block
voice Kyri
host Linux pier, 8 vCPU / 16 GB, TZ America/New_York
title What the fleet fixed by accident
prompt Keaton: kg.
think Lap N=4102, row 2 -- Fire, cut and stop, read through its sense, which is SEES. Standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal, with the threshold page first.
think Fire's own question is what should stop. Reading the rota's own page for that answer, I found a standing proposal waiting on Keaton's word since 20260825: advance the rota by lap rather than by commit, because N counts COMMITS and a lap may make two or none, so 11 rows went unread across 19 recorded lap pairs.
think My hypothesis was that eight ships sharing one counter makes this far worse -- each ship's N jumps by seven between its own laps, so each should skip two rows every time. That is a clean prediction, so I measured it rather than writing it.
obs THE PREDICTION WAS WRONG AND THE WRONGNESS IS THE FINDING. Across 105 session logs today, 68 record a rota row, and they land 11, 12, 13, 20, 12 on rows 0 through 4. Against a uniform expectation of 13.6 that is chi-squared 3.91 on 4 degrees of freedom, well under the 9.49 that would mark a real skew. The distribution is consistent with uniform.
obs WHAT BREAKS ONE SHIP'S CYCLE IS WHAT FIXES THE FLEET'S COVERAGE. Eight ships sampling a shared counter at uncorrelated moments read the corpus evenly by accident. The grid asks that every document return to living awareness roughly once a working day; at fleet scale every row is read a dozen times a day. The proposal solves a single-ship problem the fleet has already left behind, so it stays available and is no longer urgent.
obs I ALMOST SHIPPED THE OPPOSITE CLAIM. The hypothesis was plausible, the arithmetic behind it was right, and it predicted a fault that measurement does not show. Fire sees: a lens whose job is to find what must stop is exactly the lens most able to manufacture one. The chi-squared took a minute and is the difference between a finding and an invention.
obs THE GAP THE SAME READING DID FIND IS A DIFFERENT ONE. 37 of 105 logs record no rota row at all. A rota read leaving no trace cannot be counted, corrected, or trusted -- the unheard-guard shape in another room. Named rather than gated, because a lap that legitimately did no rota read looks identical to one that skipped it, and a gate that cannot tell them apart would red on honest work.
loom rota logs=105 recording_a_row=68 silent=37 rows=11,12,13,20,12 expected=13.6 chi2=3.91 df=4 critical=9.49
loom rota verdict=consistent_with_uniform proposal=available_not_urgent
file recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md the fleet-scale measurement, the proposal de-escalated, and the silent-log gap named
scope one rota lap read through fire's sense; a standing proposal measured rather than argued
status GREEN -- tracked links ok, unshared citations zero, living card ascii ok
recommend keep-going -- the silent-log gap wants a reading that can tell a skipped rota from an honest absence, which is a lap rather than a guard.
